# p_e8b3 — Standard split, v3: Guitar rests on couch overnight, dog bag on kitchen floor (fork of p_7d2a)

This fork of p_7d2a corrects two resting-place errors that the 03:00 patrol passes expose. First, Yuki's guitar is on the living-room couch at night (03:00 sightings: couch_l1 ×2, bedroom_floor_b1 ×0), not on the bedroom floor. The bedroom floor is where she plays it during her 15:00–16:30 afternoon practice (confirmed by the 18:00 sighting at bedroom_floor_b1), but between practice and the next morning the guitar lives on the couch. The p_5f1a claim (guitar at couch, 2–5 h) scored for 2, against 0, confirming this. Second, the dog food bag lives on the kitchen floor (floor_k_k1), not the pantry shelf. The 03:00, 07:00, and 08:00 sightings all place it on the floor; it appears at pantry_shelf_k1 only at 18:00 (×1) before returning to the floor by 19:00. The p_9e1f claim (pantry shelf 17–19 h) scored for 1, against 3, confirming the bag is not reliably there in that window.

Everything else from p_7d2a is retained: lunchbox and vitamins OUT_OF_HOUSE 13.5–23 h weekdays; journal at desk_b1 11–14 h weekdays, nightstand otherwise; yoga mat on the living-room floor 06:00–06:45; standard meal and TV windows; Yuki's keys, jacket, sunglasses, water bottle at the entry.

What sets this document apart from p_7d2a: at 03:00 on a weekday, guitar_yuki is at couch_l1 (not bedroom_floor_b1) and dog_food_bag_shared is at floor_k_k1 (not pantry_shelf_k1). At 15:30 the guitar is at bedroom_floor_b1 in both documents. If the robot finds the guitar on the bedroom floor at 03:00 or the dog bag on the pantry shelf at 07:00, this document is refuted on those points.

